From 5b2e7c2a101d421d7e3b9c5ca368b37c4ee10b35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:09:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] drm: apple: Tell the T8122 internal DCP the lid state

On J613 the internal panel's pipe can also drive a display on the
left-front USB-C port, but only once its panel is off: the pipe's first
DPTX core drives the panel otherwise. macOS tells the panel's IOMFB the
lid state and powers the panel off in clamshell mode; the firmware then
releases the DPTX controllers it holds for the panel. Do the same for
the internal pipe that has a Type-C route (dcp->clamshell):

- Follow the lid switch (SW_LID, the SMC's on Apple laptops) with an
  input handler, registered once the panel has started.
- Tell IOMFB the state with method A475 (one u32: 1 open, 2 closed;
  "clamshell value is %d" in the firmware): the real state from the
  start, then every change. IOMFB keeps the value and hands it to its
  DPTX power controller at each panel power-on, which refuses anything
  but 1 or 2.
- While the lid is closed, a CRTC switched off powers the panel off
  (A472(0)) after the usual black swap, and switching it on powers the
  panel on again (A472(1)) and resends the colour matrix. The desktop's
  clamshell handling decides when, as on any laptop; with the lid open
  a CRTC switched off only blanks, as before. A472(0) is sent only after
  A475(2), whichever of the lid event and the CRTC change comes first.
- No swaps go to a panel that is powered off.
- Answer what the firmware sends around those power changes: D2, D591
  and D574 as on an external processor, and D593 (four bytes, once
  after power-on, meaning not known) with nothing.

Tested on J613 in the dev series (same calls): lid closed and opened
6 times with an external display, the panel came back each time.

Other machines, and J613 without the Type-C route, are unchanged.

